<p>We're here to show you what the C++ language is and what we can use it f=
or.</p>

<p>Let=E2=80=99s consider for a moment what language itself is, not only th=
e C++ language, but any language people use. We=E2=80=99ll try not to use s=
cientific sounding definitions and we=E2=80=99ll try to speak informally. W=
e can say that <b>a language is a tool for expressing and recording human t=
houghts</b>. We really like this definition. In other words, it's a mechani=
sm known to us and to our partners, allowing us all to understand and to be=
 understood. We use language for speaking, writing, reading, listening and =
thinking.</p>

